export const privacy = "<div class=\"page-header\">\n    <a href=\"/\" class=\"brand-link\">\n      <div class=\"app-name\">SLP Command</div>\n      <div class=\"app-tag\">Independent educational preparation for STANAG&nbsp;6001 / SLP-style English exams</div>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n\n  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>\n  <p class=\"updated\">Last updated: 31 July 2026 · Controller: SLP Command · <a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a></p>\n\n  <p>This Privacy Policy explains what personal data SLP Command processes, why, on what legal basis, with whom it is shared, how long it is retained, and what rights you have under the General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (\"GDPR\") and Spanish Organic Law 3/2018 (LOPDGDD).</p>\n\n  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>\n  <p>SLP Command is the data controller responsible for the personal data described in this Policy. Contact: <a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a>. Full controller identification data is available in the <a href=\"/legal-notice\">Legal Notice</a>.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. Categories of personal data we process</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Account data:</strong> your email address and a password hash (passwords are managed by our authentication provider — we never store them in plain text).</li>\n    <li><strong>Learning content:</strong> written responses (Writing), audio recordings (Speaking — optional, consent-based), and AI-generated transcripts of that audio.</li>\n    <li><strong>Performance data:</strong> scores, estimated SLP levels, exercise history, and the derived Adaptive Coach / Intelligence Dashboard insights.</li>\n    <li><strong>Support data:</strong> if you submit a report via \"Report a Problem\", we process the category and free-text description you provide, together with your app version, iOS version, and the screen name.</li>\n    <li><strong>Subscription and purchase data:</strong> if you subscribe to SLP Command Professional, we process a technical subscriber identifier linked to your account, the App Store product identifier, App Store transaction identifiers, subscription status, and purchase/renewal/expiration dates. This information reaches us through RevenueCat, our subscription-management technology provider — see §4. We do not receive or store your payment card number or other full payment credentials; your payment itself is handled directly by Apple as an independent party, not by us — see §4a.</li>\n    <li><strong>Product usage data:</strong> pseudonymous, event-level analytics describing which features and screens you use (e.g. module opened, quiz completed, exam started), your app version, and a pseudonymous user identifier. This data <strong>never</strong> includes your written answers, audio, transcripts, or any content you submit.</li>\n    <li><strong>Technical &amp; security data:</strong> a pseudonymous user identifier, IP address (processed transiently for rate-limiting and abuse prevention, and stored in hashed, non-reversible form in our security audit trail — see §6.5), device/app version, and crash or error diagnostics stripped of personal content.</li>\n    <li><strong>Security audit trail:</strong> a limited, append-only log of security-relevant account events (e.g. login, account creation, account deletion) associated with a pseudonymous user identifier and a hashed IP address, retained according to the schedule in §6.5.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect your name, postal address, phone number, government identifiers, location data, advertising identifiers, military rank, unit, service branch, or employer. We do <strong>not</strong> track you across other apps or websites.</p>\n\n  <h2>3. Legal bases for processing (Article 6 GDPR)</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Performance of a contract (Art. 6.1.b):</strong> account provisioning, progress synchronisation, delivery of exercises, Writing feedback, score history, and the Adaptive Coach / Intelligence Dashboard.</li>\n    <li><strong>Explicit consent (Art. 6.1.a):</strong> processing your Speaking audio for transcription and AI evaluation. This consent is requested separately, in context, before your first use of the Speaking feature, and is entirely optional — you can use every other feature of the Service without ever granting it. You may withdraw it at any time.</li>\n    <li><strong>Legitimate interest (Art. 6.1.f):</strong> maintaining the security, stability, integrity and abuse-resistance of the Service, and understanding aggregate, pseudonymous product usage to improve it.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>4. Sub-processors</h2>\n  <p>To deliver the Service, we share personal data with the following processors, each bound by a data processing agreement requiring it to act only on our instructions. See the full <a href=\"/subprocessors\">Subprocessors and Third Parties</a> page for details.</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — serves and protects slpcommand.com, and is the runtime the web application runs on. Every request to the website passes through Cloudflare, which therefore processes your IP address, request metadata and — in transit — the contents of those requests and responses, including your session cookie.</li>\n    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — database, authentication, audio file storage.</li>\n    <li><strong>OpenAI</strong> — Whisper (speech-to-text transcription) and GPT models (evaluation of Speaking and Writing responses across fluency, grammar, vocabulary, coherence and task achievement).</li>\n    <li><strong>ElevenLabs</strong> — text-to-speech audio generation for listening exercises and pronunciation models (exercise text only, no personal data), and the live AI Speaking Coach, which is an optional spoken conversation you enter only after giving explicit consent and during which your microphone audio is processed in real time.</li>\n    <li><strong>xAI (Grok)</strong> — the in-app support assistant. Only the messages you write in a support conversation, and the replies to them, are processed. It is never used to evaluate or score your work, and receives none of your exam answers, audio or results.</li>\n    <li><strong>Render</strong> — backend API hosting.</li>\n    <li><strong>Sentry</strong> — crash and error diagnostics. Request bodies and authorization headers are stripped before transmission; no personal content or audio is sent to Sentry.</li>\n    <li><strong>PostHog</strong> — pseudonymous product usage analytics (feature/screen usage, app version). Never your written answers, audio, transcripts, or account email.</li>\n    <li><strong>RevenueCat</strong> — subscription-management technology provider; validates your App Store purchase and tracks subscription status so the app can grant Professional-plan access.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>We do not sell your personal data to any third party. We do not permit AI providers to use your Content to train their general-purpose models, except where you have given separate, explicit consent.</p>\n\n  <h2>4a. Apple — an independent party, not our processor</h2>\n  <p>Apple Inc. operates the App Store, through which the app is distributed and through which any subscription purchase is made. For that purchase, Apple is <strong>not</strong> a processor acting on our instructions: Apple determines the purposes and means of processing your payment, your Apple ID, and your purchase history itself, under Apple's own <a href=\"https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/\">Privacy Policy</a>. We only receive, via RevenueCat, the limited technical information described in §2 above — never your full payment details.</p>\n\n  <h2>5. International transfers</h2>\n  <p>Some of the providers listed above process data outside the European Economic Area, principally in the United States. Where this occurs, transfers rely on appropriate safeguards under Article 46 GDPR, including the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses and, where applicable, provider participation in the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.</p>\n\n  <h2>6. Retention</h2>\n  <p>See the full <a href=\"/data-retention\">Data Retention Policy</a> for the itemised schedule. Summary:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Account, progress, scores, transcripts, written responses:</strong> retained for the life of your account, then permanently deleted within 30 days of account deletion.</li>\n    <li><strong>Speaking audio recordings:</strong> retained only while you keep them. You can delete individual recordings from the App at any time. All audio is permanently removed when you delete your account.</li>\n    <li><strong>Support requests:</strong> retained for 12 months from submission, or until account deletion, whichever comes first.</li>\n    <li><strong>Diagnostic / crash logs:</strong> retained short-term only (typically 30–90 days).</li>\n    <li><strong>Subscription and billing records:</strong> while your account is active, we keep the subscription data described in §2. If you delete your account, the identifiers linking those records to you are removed and the remaining technical/financial fields are kept, dissociated from your account, only for as long as necessary for the purposes described in §3 of the <a href=\"/data-retention\">Data Retention Policy</a>.</li>\n    <li><strong>Security audit trail (§6.5):</strong> by exception, security-relevant events (login, account creation, account deletion, administrative actions) are retained for <strong>12 months from the date of the event, irrespective of account deletion</strong>, on the basis of our legitimate interest (Art. 6.1.f) in investigating fraud, abuse and security incidents. This entry never contains your email, written content, audio or transcripts — only event type, a pseudonymous identifier, a hashed IP address, and a timestamp. Once your account is deleted, this identifier no longer resolves to any identifiable individual within our systems. Every entry is automatically and permanently purged 12 months after creation.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>7. Your rights (EEA / UK — GDPR / LOPDGDD)</h2>\n  <p>You have the right to <strong>access</strong>, <strong>rectify</strong>, <strong>erase</strong>, <strong>restrict</strong>, <strong>object to</strong>, and <strong>port</strong> your data. To exercise any of these rights, contact <a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a>. We will respond within one month, extendable by two further months for complex requests. You may also lodge a complaint with your supervisory authority — in Spain, the <a href=\"https://www.aepd.es\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AEPD</a>.</p>\n  <p>In-app account deletion is available from <strong>Settings → Delete Account</strong>. See <a href=\"/delete-account\">Delete Account</a> for full details.</p>\n\n  <h2>8. Automated decision-making</h2>\n  <p>The Intelligence Dashboard and Adaptive Coach are computed exclusively from your own historical results within the Service. They do not produce any decision with legal or similarly significant effect on you within the meaning of Article 22 GDPR: they are non-binding, educational recommendations. See the <a href=\"/ai-usage\">Responsible AI Policy</a>.</p>\n\n  <h2>9. Audio data and biometrics</h2>\n  <p>Audio recordings are processed solely for speech-to-text transcription and language evaluation. We do not use audio to identify you biometrically. Audio is classified as personal data under GDPR but not as a biometric identifier (Art. 9) because it is not processed for the purpose of unique identification.</p>\n\n  <h2>10. Children</h2>\n  <p>The Service is not directed at individuals under 16 years of age. If we become aware that we have collected personal data from a person under 16 without a valid legal basis, we will delete that data. Contact <a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a> if you believe this has occurred.</p>\n\n  <h2>11. Security</h2>\n  <p>See the <a href=\"/security\">Security Policy</a> for the full statement of technical and organisational measures.</p>\n\n  <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>\n  <p>We may update this Policy from time to time. Material changes affecting the sub-processors in §4 or the retention schedule in §6 will be notified via the Service or by email at least 15 days before taking effect.</p>\n\n  <h2>13. Contact</h2>\n  <p><a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a></p>\n\n  <footer class=\"page-footer\">\n    <a href=\"/\">← SLP Command</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Not affiliated with NATO or any official body.\n  </footer>";

export const terms = "<div class=\"page-header\">\n    <a href=\"/\" class=\"brand-link\">\n      <div class=\"app-name\">SLP Command</div>\n      <div class=\"app-tag\">Independent educational preparation for STANAG&nbsp;6001 / SLP-style English exams</div>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n\n  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>\n  <p class=\"updated\">Last updated: 31 July 2026</p>\n\n  <p>These Terms of Service (\"Terms\") constitute a legally binding agreement between you (\"User\", \"you\") and SLP Command (\"we\", \"us\", \"our\") governing your access to and use of the SLP Command mobile application and associated services (collectively, the \"Service\").</p>\n  <p><strong>By creating an account, you affirmatively accept these Terms. If you do not agree, do not create an account or use the Service.</strong></p>\n\n  <h2>1. Definitions</h2>\n  <p><strong>\"Service\"</strong> means the SLP Command mobile application, backend infrastructure, and all associated features (Reading, Listening, Writing, Speaking, Academy, Intelligence Dashboard, Adaptive Coach, Exam Simulation). <strong>\"Content\"</strong> means any text, audio, or other material submitted by a User through the Service. <strong>\"AI Feedback\"</strong> means automated evaluations, scores, transcriptions or estimated proficiency levels generated by artificial intelligence systems integrated into the Service. <strong>\"Official Assessment\"</strong> means a certified, binding evaluation of English language proficiency issued by an authorised examining body under the STANAG&nbsp;6001 framework or an equivalent official qualification system.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. Who we are</h2>\n  <p>SLP Command is an independent educational technology platform operated in Spain. We are not affiliated with NATO, any Ministry of Defence, any armed forces, or any official examining body. See <a href=\"/disclaimer\">Disclaimer</a>.</p>\n\n  <h2>3. Educational purpose — no official assessment</h2>\n  <p>The Service provides <strong>independent, self-directed educational preparation</strong> for STANAG&nbsp;6001 / SLP-style English examinations. The Service does <strong>not</strong>: (a) issue any Official Assessment, certificate, or accreditation; (b) guarantee that use of the Service will result in passing any official exam; (c) substitute for evaluation by a certified human examiner. Estimated SLP levels, scores, readiness indicators and all AI Feedback are indicative, educational, and non-binding. You acknowledge that any academic, professional, administrative or career decision made in reliance on the Service is made at your sole discretion and risk.</p>\n\n  <h2>4. Eligibility</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>You must be at least 16 years old to create an account and use the Service.</li>\n    <li>You must provide accurate registration information and maintain the security of your account credentials.</li>\n    <li>One account per person. Account sharing or resale of access is prohibited.</li>\n    <li>If we become aware that an account was created by a person under 16 without a valid legal basis, we reserve the right to suspend the account and delete the associated personal data.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>5. Account registration and security</h2>\n  <p>You are responsible for all activity occurring under your account. You must notify us immediately at <a href=\"mailto:security@slpcommand.com\">security@slpcommand.com</a> if you suspect unauthorised access to your account.</p>\n\n  <h2>6. AI-generated feedback</h2>\n  <p>Speaking and Writing feedback is generated using OpenAI Whisper (speech-to-text) and GPT models (evaluation). AI Feedback may contain errors, omissions, or inconsistencies. Processing of your Speaking audio for AI evaluation is based on your explicit, separately-obtained consent (see the <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>). You may withdraw this consent at any time by discontinuing use of the Speaking feature. See the <a href=\"/ai-usage\">Responsible AI Policy</a> for the full transparency statement required under Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 (the \"AI Act\").</p>\n\n  <h2>7. Your content</h2>\n  <p>You retain all ownership rights in the text and audio Content you submit. You grant SLP Command a limited, non-exclusive, revocable licence to process your Content solely to: generate AI Feedback; maintain your score history and progress records; power the Adaptive Coach and Intelligence Dashboard; and provide customer support in connection with content you submit through \"Report a Problem\". We do not use your Content to train or fine-tune artificial intelligence models, and we do not sell, license or otherwise commercially exploit your Content, without your prior explicit consent. You represent that you own or have the necessary rights to any Content you submit.</p>\n\n  <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>\n  <p>You agree to use the Service for lawful, personal, non-commercial study purposes only. You must not:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Upload unlawful, defamatory, obscene, or third-party copyrighted content without authorisation.</li>\n    <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload, probe, scan, or reverse-engineer the Service or its underlying infrastructure.</li>\n    <li>Attempt to extract, scrape, or systematically download the question corpus, exercise content, or any structured dataset from the Service.</li>\n    <li>Circumvent, disable, or interfere with any security-related feature of the Service.</li>\n    <li>Share your account credentials or resell, sublicense, or otherwise provide third-party access without prior written consent.</li>\n    <li>Use the Service for any commercial, institutional or resale purpose without a separate written agreement.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>\n  <p>The Service, including its software, source code, question corpus, exercise content, audio assets, scoring algorithms, adaptive-learning methodology, dashboard design, and all associated trademarks, is the exclusive intellectual property of SLP Command and is protected under applicable intellectual property law. See the <a href=\"/intellectual-property\">Intellectual Property Policy</a> for full terms. Nothing in these Terms transfers any intellectual property right to you except the limited licence to use the Service as intended.</p>\n\n  <h2>10. Fees and subscriptions</h2>\n  <p>The Service is available on a Free plan and on a paid \"SLP Command Professional\" plan, offered as an auto-renewable subscription purchased through the Apple App Store.</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Price and billing period:</strong> the price and billing period presented to you are those shown by Apple at the point of purchase — this document does not state a fixed amount, because the price you are charged is the one Apple displays to you before you confirm the purchase, and may vary by country, region, currency, applicable taxes and App Store storefront.</li>\n    <li><strong>Auto-renewal:</strong> the subscription renews automatically for successive periods of the same length unless you turn off auto-renewal at least 24 hours before the end of the current billing period. Your Apple ID account is charged for renewal within the 24 hours preceding the end of the current period, at the then-current price shown by Apple.</li>\n    <li><strong>Managing or cancelling:</strong> you can manage or cancel your subscription at any time from your Apple ID account settings (Settings → [your name] → Subscriptions on your device), or from the \"Manage Subscription\" option inside the app, which opens that same Apple screen. Cancellation stops future renewals but does not refund the current, already-paid period.</li>\n    <li><strong>Deleting the app or your SLP Command account does not, by itself, cancel an active Apple subscription.</strong> Because the subscription is billed and administered by Apple through your Apple ID, it continues to renew until you cancel it directly through Apple, even if you delete the SLP Command app or your SLP Command account.</li>\n    <li><strong>Payment processing:</strong> your payment is handled by Apple as part of the App Store purchase flow. SLP Command does not receive or store your card number or other full payment credentials. SLP Command relies on RevenueCat, a subscription-management technology provider, to validate purchases with Apple and keep track of your subscription status (active, expired, renewed, cancelled) so that Professional-plan access can be granted or withdrawn accordingly — see <a href=\"/subprocessors\">Subprocessors and Third Parties</a> for the categories of data involved.</li>\n    <li><strong>Restore Purchases:</strong> if you reinstall the app or sign in on a new device with the same Apple ID, use \"Restore Purchases\" (available on the paywall and in Settings) to restore an active subscription without being charged again.</li>\n    <li><strong>Refunds:</strong> refund requests are submitted to and decided by Apple under Apple's own refund policy; SLP Command has no ability to issue a refund directly, since it does not process or hold your payment.</li>\n    <li><strong>What happens when the Professional period ends:</strong> once your subscription expires or is cancelled and the current period ends, your account reverts to the Free plan. Practice history, scores and progress already recorded are not deleted, but the additional volume, feedback and exam-simulation allowances reserved for the Professional plan are no longer available until you resubscribe.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>SLP Command reserves the right to change the price applicable to future billing periods, or to introduce additional paid tiers; any such change will be presented to you through the App Store before it takes effect on you, and will never be applied retroactively to a period you have already paid for.</p>\n\n  <h2>11. Service availability</h2>\n  <p>The Service is provided on an \"as is\" and \"as available\" basis. SLP Command does not warrant uninterrupted, error-free, or continuously available operation. We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any part of the Service at any time, with reasonable notice where practicable.</p>\n\n  <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>\n  <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, SLP Command shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including loss of opportunity, loss of income, or adverse exam, employment, or administrative outcomes arising from your use of or reliance on the Service or any AI Feedback. SLP Command's total aggregate liability arising out of or related to these Terms shall not exceed the amount paid by you to SLP Command in the twelve (12) months preceding the event giving rise to the claim, or EUR&nbsp;100 if no amount has been paid. Nothing in this clause excludes or limits liability for death, personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or any other liability that cannot be excluded or limited under applicable law, including mandatory EU and Spanish consumer-protection law.</p>\n\n  <h2>13. Termination</h2>\n  <p>You may stop using the Service and delete your account at any time from <strong>Settings → Delete Account</strong>. See <a href=\"/delete-account\">Delete Account</a>. We may suspend or terminate your account, with notice where practicable, if you breach these Terms, engage in fraudulent or abusive conduct, or if required to do so by law. Sections 7, 9, 12 and 17 survive termination.</p>\n\n  <h2>14. Changes to these Terms</h2>\n  <p>We may amend these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be notified via the Service or by email at least 15 days before taking effect, except where a shorter period is required by law or necessary to address a security issue. Continued use after the effective date constitutes acceptance.</p>\n\n  <h2>15. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>\n  <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of Spain. Without prejudice to any mandatory jurisdiction applicable to you as a consumer under Regulation (EU) No 1215/2012, disputes shall be submitted to the courts of Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, Spain.</p>\n\n  <h2>16. Relationship with Apple's Standard EULA</h2>\n  <p>Because you download the app through the Apple App Store, Apple's <a href=\"https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/\">Standard End User License Agreement (EULA)</a> also applies to your use of the app, alongside these Terms. These Terms govern the Service SLP Command provides (educational content, features, subscriptions, your account); the Apple Standard EULA governs your licence to use the app as software distributed through the App Store. If a specific provision of these Terms conflicts with a mandatory provision of the Apple Standard EULA or with Apple's own App Store terms, the provision required by the applicable platform terms or by mandatory law will prevail for that specific point, without affecting the validity of the remainder of these Terms.</p>\n\n  <h2>17. Miscellaneous</h2>\n  <p>If any provision of these Terms is held invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in full force. These Terms, together with the <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href=\"/ai-usage\">Responsible AI Policy</a>, <a href=\"/cookies\">Cookie Policy</a>, and <a href=\"/disclaimer\">Institutional Disclaimer</a>, constitute the entire agreement between you and SLP Command regarding the Service (without prejudice to the Apple Standard EULA referenced in §16, which governs your licence to the app as distributed software). Failure to enforce any right does not constitute a waiver of that right.</p>\n\n  <h2>18. Contact</h2>\n  <p><a href=\"mailto:legal@slpcommand.com\">legal@slpcommand.com</a></p>\n\n  <footer class=\"page-footer\">\n    <a href=\"/\">← SLP Command</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Not affiliated with NATO or any official body.\n  </footer>";

export const ai_usage = "<div class=\"page-header\">\n    <a href=\"/\" class=\"brand-link\">\n      <div class=\"app-name\">SLP Command</div>\n      <div class=\"app-tag\">Independent educational preparation for STANAG&nbsp;6001 / SLP-style English exams</div>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n\n  <h1>Responsible AI Policy</h1>\n  <p class=\"updated\">Last updated: 12 July 2026</p>\n\n  <p>This Policy explains, in accordance with the transparency obligations of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 (the \"AI Act\") and Articles 13–14 GDPR, which artificial intelligence systems SLP Command uses, what they receive, their limitations, and the human oversight applied to them.</p>\n\n  <h2>1. AI systems in use</h2>\n\n  <h3>OpenAI — Whisper (transcription)</h3>\n  <p>When you record a Speaking response, your audio is sent to OpenAI's Whisper model for speech-to-text transcription. The resulting transcript is used as input for evaluation.</p>\n\n  <h3>OpenAI — GPT (evaluation)</h3>\n  <p>Your Speaking transcripts and Writing responses are evaluated by OpenAI GPT models. Evaluation covers:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Fluency</strong> — smoothness, pace, and naturalness of delivery.</li>\n    <li><strong>Grammar</strong> — accuracy of grammatical structures.</li>\n    <li><strong>Vocabulary</strong> — range and appropriateness of lexical choices.</li>\n    <li><strong>Coherence</strong> — logical organisation and clarity of ideas.</li>\n    <li><strong>Task Achievement</strong> — how fully the response addresses the prompt.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>ElevenLabs — Text-to-Speech</h3>\n  <p>Listening exercises and pronunciation models are generated using ElevenLabs text-to-speech technology, from exercise text only. No personal data is sent to ElevenLabs.</p>\n\n  <h3>ElevenLabs — live AI Speaking Coach</h3>\n  <p>The <strong>live AI Speaking Coach</strong> is a spoken conversation with an AI agent, provided by ElevenLabs. It is optional, is entered only after you give explicit consent on the consent screen, and is separate from recorded Speaking Practice. During a session your microphone audio and the agent's spoken replies pass through ElevenLabs in order to hold the conversation in real time.</p>\n\n  <h3>xAI (Grok) — in-app support assistant</h3>\n  <p>When you open a support conversation inside the app or on the website, the messages you write and the assistant's replies are processed by xAI's Grok model to produce an answer. This is used <strong>only</strong> for support. It plays no part in evaluating, scoring or assessing your work, and it does not receive your exam answers, your Speaking audio or your scores.</p>\n\n  <h3>Adaptive recommendations and the Intelligence Dashboard</h3>\n  <p>The recommendation engine and the Intelligence Dashboard — what to practise next, weakness profiles, mastery and readiness — are <strong>not</strong> powered by external AI inference. They are deterministic statistical computations performed on your own historical results within our own infrastructure.</p>\n  <p class=\"legal-note\">This paragraph previously read \"Adaptive Coach and Intelligence Dashboard\". That wording could be read as covering the live AI Speaking Coach described above, which <em>is</em> external AI inference. The heading has been made specific so the two cannot be confused.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. What each AI system receives</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Speaking (recorded practice and exams):</strong> your audio recording and the exercise prompt text.</li>\n    <li><strong>Speaking (live AI Coach):</strong> your microphone audio and the agent's replies, in real time, for the duration of the session, plus the session's practice objective.</li>\n    <li><strong>Writing:</strong> your written response and the task prompt.</li>\n    <li><strong>Listening generation:</strong> exercise text only — no personal data.</li>\n    <li><strong>Support assistant:</strong> the messages you write in that support conversation and the replies to them. Nothing else from your account is sent.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>We do <strong>not</strong> send your name, email address, account identifier, or any other directly identifying information to an AI provider together with your Content.</p>\n\n  <h2>3. AI Act risk classification statement</h2>\n  <p>SLP Command has assessed whether its AI-based evaluation features fall within Annex III of the AI Act (high-risk AI systems used for the evaluation of learning outcomes).</p>\n  <p>Our conclusion, reviewed as of the date of this Policy, is that the Service does <strong>not</strong> constitute a high-risk AI system under Annex III, because:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>all AI Feedback is explicitly, consistently, and prominently disclaimed throughout the Service as indicative, non-binding, educational guidance, never as an Official Assessment;</li>\n    <li>no admission, certification, employment, promotion, or other legally or similarly significant decision about you is made, wholly or partly, based on AI Feedback generated by the Service;</li>\n    <li>the Service is used exclusively for individual, self-directed study, and is not integrated into any institutional admission, evaluation, or certification process.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>This classification is reviewed whenever the Service's use context changes materially — in particular, before any institutional, governmental, or academy-facing deployment in which AI Feedback could feed into a real admission, certification, or personnel decision. Should such a deployment occur, SLP Command commits to re-conducting this assessment and, if the high-risk threshold is met, implementing the corresponding obligations under Articles 9–15 of the AI Act before that deployment goes live.</p>\n\n  <h2>4. Transparency obligations (Article 50 AI Act)</h2>\n  <p>You are informed, both in this Policy and at the point of interaction within the Service, that you are interacting with an AI system when receiving Speaking or Writing feedback. AI-generated transcripts and evaluations are clearly labelled as such within the Service interface.</p>\n\n  <h2>5. Important limitations</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>AI feedback is <strong>indicative guidance, not an official SLP / STANAG&nbsp;6001 assessment</strong>.</li>\n    <li>AI models may produce inaccurate, inconsistent, or incomplete evaluations.</li>\n    <li>Scores and estimated levels shown in the App <strong>do not predict or guarantee</strong> any outcome in an official exam.</li>\n    <li>AI systems reflect the biases present in their training data. Always consult official examiners and materials for real exam preparation decisions.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>6. Human oversight</h2>\n  <p>SLP Command reviews aggregate AI Feedback quality on an ongoing basis and maintains a \"Report a Problem\" channel through which any user may flag inaccurate or inappropriate AI output for human review. No automated system within the Service takes any action against a user's account, access, or standing based solely on AI Feedback content.</p>\n\n  <h2>7. Data and your rights</h2>\n  <p>Your audio and text are processed by AI providers acting as sub-processors under data processing agreements. For full details on retention, deletion, and your GDPR rights, see the <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href=\"/subprocessors\">Subprocessors</a> page.</p>\n\n  <h2>8. Contact</h2>\n  <p>To report an AI-related error or concern: <a href=\"mailto:support@slpcommand.com\">support@slpcommand.com</a>. For AI Act or governance queries: <a href=\"mailto:legal@slpcommand.com\">legal@slpcommand.com</a>.</p>\n\n  <footer class=\"page-footer\">\n    <a href=\"/\">← SLP Command</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Not affiliated with NATO or any official body.\n  </footer>";

export const security = "<div class=\"page-header\">\n    <a href=\"/\" class=\"brand-link\">\n      <div class=\"app-name\">SLP Command</div>\n      <div class=\"app-tag\">Independent educational preparation for STANAG&nbsp;6001 / SLP-style English exams</div>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n\n  <h1>Security Policy</h1>\n  <p class=\"updated\">Last updated: 12 July 2026</p>\n\n  <p>This Policy describes the technical and organisational measures SLP Command applies to protect the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of user data, in accordance with Article 32 GDPR.</p>\n\n  <h2>1. Authentication and access control</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>User authentication is managed by a dedicated, industry-standard authentication provider. Passwords are never stored or transmitted in plain text; they are managed exclusively by our authentication provider using industry-standard hashing.</li>\n    <li>All requests to protected endpoints require a verified authentication token. Requests without a valid token are rejected.</li>\n    <li>Administrative access to operational dashboards requires both a verified user identity and an explicit administrator role, independently checked on every request. Administrative privileges are not self-assignable through any user-facing interface.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>2. Data isolation</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Row-Level Security (RLS) is enforced at the database layer across all tables containing user data, ensuring that a user can only access their own records, independent of application-layer logic.</li>\n    <li>Security-sensitive tables (including the security audit trail) grant zero direct read or write access to client applications; they are accessible exclusively through server-side, privilege-checked processes.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>3. Encryption</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>All data in transit between the application, our backend, and our sub-processors is encrypted using TLS/HTTPS.</li>\n    <li>Data at rest is encrypted by our infrastructure and database providers in accordance with their respective security certifications.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>4. Abuse and rate limiting</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>API rate limiting is applied to reduce the risk of automated abuse, scraping, and credential-stuffing attacks.</li>\n    <li>Failed authentication attempts and other security-relevant events are recorded in a dedicated, access-restricted security audit trail (see the <a href=\"/data-retention\">Data Retention Policy</a>).</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>5. Vulnerability and error monitoring</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Application errors and crashes are monitored through a dedicated diagnostics provider. Request bodies and authorization headers are stripped before transmission to this provider; no personal content, audio, or written responses are ever included in diagnostic data.</li>\n    <li>We conduct periodic internal security reviews of new features before release, including authentication, authorisation, and data-exposure checks.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>6. Responsible disclosure</h2>\n  <p>If you believe you have discovered a security vulnerability in the Service, please report it responsibly to <a href=\"mailto:security@slpcommand.com\">security@slpcommand.com</a>. We commit to:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>acknowledging your report within 5 business days;</li>\n    <li>investigating in good faith and keeping you informed of material progress;</li>\n    <li>not pursuing legal action against good-faith security researchers who report vulnerabilities through this channel without exploiting them beyond what is necessary to demonstrate the issue.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>7. Incident response</h2>\n  <p>In the event of a personal data breach likely to result in a risk to your rights and freedoms, we will notify the competent supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming aware of the breach, in accordance with Article 33 GDPR, and will notify affected users without undue delay where the breach is likely to result in a high risk to their rights and freedoms, in accordance with Article 34 GDPR.</p>\n\n  <h2>8. Sub-processor security</h2>\n  <p>We select sub-processors that maintain industry-recognised security practices and are bound by data processing agreements requiring appropriate technical and organisational measures. See the <a href=\"/subprocessors\">Subprocessors</a> page for the complete list.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"note\">SLP Command will never ask for your password by email, support chat, or any channel other than the official in-app login screen.</div>\n\n  <h2>9. Contact</h2>\n  <p><a href=\"mailto:security@slpcommand.com\">security@slpcommand.com</a></p>\n\n  <footer class=\"page-footer\">\n    <a href=\"/\">← SLP Command</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Not affiliated with NATO or any official body.\n  </footer>";

export const cookies = "<div class=\"page-header\">\n    <a href=\"/\" class=\"brand-link\">\n      <div class=\"app-name\">SLP Command</div>\n      <div class=\"app-tag\">Independent educational preparation for STANAG&nbsp;6001 / SLP-style English exams</div>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n\n  <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>\n  <p class=\"updated\">Last updated: 16 August 2026</p>\n\n  <h2>1. Scope</h2>\n  <p>This Cookie Policy applies to the website located at slpcommand.com. The SLP Command mobile application does not use browser cookies; on-device analytics storage used by the mobile app is described in the <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>, §2.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. What are cookies</h2>\n  <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They can be used for technical, analytical, or advertising purposes.</p>\n\n  <h2>3. Cookies used on this website</h2>\n  <p>As of the date of this Policy, slpcommand.com uses <strong>only</strong> strictly necessary technical cookies or equivalent local storage mechanisms required for the basic functioning of the website (authentication of the learner application and of the administrative console). We do <strong>not</strong> use:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>advertising or marketing cookies;</li>\n    <li>behavioural tracking or cross-site profiling cookies;</li>\n    <li>third-party analytics cookies on the public website.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>Because we do not use non-essential cookies, no cookie-consent banner is required under Article 22.2 of the LSSI-CE, per the guidance of the Spanish Data Protection Agency (Agencia Española de Protección de Datos, \"AEPD\") — consent is only required for cookies that are not strictly necessary for the service requested by the user.</p>\n\n  <h2>4. Table of cookies / equivalent storage</h2>\n  <div class=\"legal-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"legal-table\">\n    <tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th><th>Party</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>adminViewMode</td><td>Strictly necessary preference (local storage)</td><td>Remembers Simple vs Advanced on the administrative dashboard</td><td>Until cleared</td><td>First party</td><td>Art. 22.2 LSSI-CE exemption</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>slp_at</td><td>Strictly necessary authentication cookie (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax, Path=/)</td><td>Short-lived access token so the website can call the SLP Command API on your behalf, including the administrative console. Never readable by page JavaScript</td><td>Approximately 1 hour</td><td>First party</td><td>Art. 22.2 LSSI-CE exemption</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>slp_rt</td><td>Strictly necessary authentication cookie (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax, Path=/api)</td><td>Refresh token used only by our own /api routes to renew slp_at. Never readable by page JavaScript</td><td>Approximately 14 days</td><td>First party</td><td>Art. 22.2 LSSI-CE exemption</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>slp_uid, slp_em</td><td>Strictly necessary authentication cookies (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax)</td><td>Account identifier and email so the website can restore your session after reload without exposing tokens</td><td>Approximately 14 days</td><td>First party</td><td>Art. 22.2 LSSI-CE exemption</td></tr>\n  </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2>5. If this changes</h2>\n  <p>Should we introduce analytics or marketing cookies in the future, we will update this Policy and implement a consent banner offering clear options to <strong>Accept</strong>, <strong>Reject</strong>, and <strong>Configure</strong> your preferences, in accordance with AEPD guidance, before any non-essential cookie is set.</p>\n\n  <h2>6. How to control cookies at browser level</h2>\n  <p>You may disable or delete cookies at any time through your browser settings. Disabling strictly necessary cookies may affect the availability of the administrative dashboard.</p>\n\n  <h2>7. Contact</h2>\n  <p><a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a></p>\n\n  <footer class=\"page-footer\">\n    <a href=\"/\">← SLP Command</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Not affiliated with NATO or any official body.\n  </footer>";

export const data_retention = "<div class=\"page-header\">\n    <a href=\"/\" class=\"brand-link\">\n      <div class=\"app-name\">SLP Command</div>\n      <div class=\"app-tag\">Independent educational preparation for STANAG&nbsp;6001 / SLP-style English exams</div>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n\n  <h1>Data Retention Policy</h1>\n  <p class=\"updated\">Last updated: 31 July 2026</p>\n\n  <p>This Policy sets out, in accordance with the storage-limitation principle of Article&nbsp;5(1)(e) GDPR, exactly how long each category of personal data processed by SLP Command is retained, and what happens to it thereafter.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"legal-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"legal-table\">\n    <tr><th>Data category</th><th>Retention period</th><th>Trigger for deletion</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>Account credentials (email, password hash)</td><td>Life of account</td><td>Deleted within 30 days of account deletion</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Written responses (Writing)</td><td>Life of account</td><td>Deleted within 30 days of account deletion</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Speaking audio recordings</td><td>Until deleted by user, or life of account</td><td>Individually deletable at any time; permanently deleted within 30 days of account deletion</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>AI-generated transcripts</td><td>Life of account</td><td>Deleted within 30 days of account deletion</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Scores, estimated levels, exercise history</td><td>Life of account</td><td>Deleted within 30 days of account deletion</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Adaptive Coach / Intelligence Dashboard data</td><td>Life of account</td><td>Deleted within 30 days of account deletion</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Support requests (\"Report a Problem\")</td><td>12 months, or life of account, whichever is sooner</td><td>Automatically purged after 12 months; deleted immediately on account deletion where already resolved</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Product usage analytics (pseudonymous)</td><td>Up to 12 months</td><td>Automatically aged out; not linked back to your account identity after deletion</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Crash / error diagnostics</td><td>30–90 days</td><td>Automatically purged by our diagnostics provider</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Security audit trail</td><td><strong>12 months from the event, irrespective of account deletion</strong></td><td>Automatically and permanently purged 12 months after creation</td></tr>\n  </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2>1. General principle</h2>\n  <p>Except for the security audit trail described in §2, all personal data associated with your account is permanently deleted within 30 days of a verified account deletion request, in accordance with your right to erasure under Article&nbsp;17 GDPR.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. The security audit trail exception</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>A limited set of security-relevant events (account login, account creation, account deletion, administrative actions performed on your account) is retained for 12 months from the date of the event, even after you delete your account.</li>\n    <li>This exception exists on the basis of our legitimate interest (Article&nbsp;6.1.f GDPR) in investigating fraud, unauthorised access, and security incidents that may only come to light after an account has already been deleted (for example, a compromised account deleted by an attacker to conceal unauthorised access).</li>\n    <li>This log entry contains <strong>only</strong>: an event type, a pseudonymous user identifier, a hashed (non-reversible) IP address, and a timestamp. It never contains your email address, written content, audio, or transcripts.</li>\n    <li>Once your account is deleted, the pseudonymous identifier retained in this log no longer resolves to any identifiable individual within our systems — it cannot, on its own, be used to re-identify you.</li>\n    <li>Every entry in the security audit trail is automatically and permanently purged exactly 12 months after its creation, with no exception and no manual extension process.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>3. Retention of subscription and billing records</h2>\n  <p>SLP Command may retain certain minimal technical and transactional records, duly dissociated from your account, where necessary for the reconciliation of transactions, the prevention of fraud, the handling of claims, defence against liability, or compliance with an applicable legal obligation. These records are retained only for as long as necessary for those purposes.</p>\n  <p>Specifically: when you delete your account, your subscription/billing event records are <strong>not</strong> deleted outright. Instead, the identifiers capable of linking those records back to you within our systems — your account identifier and the RevenueCat subscriber identifier, alias and subscriber-attribute fields embedded in them — are irreversibly removed. The record that remains keeps only technical and financial fields relevant to the transaction itself (product purchased, price, currency, an App Store transaction identifier, and dates); it no longer contains your email address, learning content, or audio.</p>\n  <p>We describe this record as <strong>dissociated from your account</strong> rather than as fully \"anonymised\" in the strict sense: the App Store transaction identifier that remains is, in principle, capable of being linked back to a specific purchase by Apple or RevenueCat within their own systems, even though it can no longer be linked to you within SLP Command's own systems once your account no longer exists.</p>\n\n  <h2>4. Your rights</h2>\n  <p>You may request early deletion, access, or portability of any data described in this Policy at any time by contacting <a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a>, subject to the security audit trail exception described in §2, which cannot be shortened on request because its purpose is specifically to survive account deletion for security-investigation purposes.</p>\n\n  <h2>5. Contact</h2>\n  <p><a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a></p>\n\n  <footer class=\"page-footer\">\n    <a href=\"/\">← SLP Command</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Not affiliated with NATO or any official body.\n  </footer>";

export const delete_account = "<div class=\"page-header\">\n    <a href=\"/\" class=\"brand-link\">\n      <div class=\"app-name\">SLP Command</div>\n      <div class=\"app-tag\">Independent educational preparation for STANAG&nbsp;6001 / SLP-style English exams</div>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n\n  <h1>Account Deletion Policy</h1>\n  <p class=\"updated\">Last updated: 31 July 2026</p>\n\n  <p>You can request deletion of your account and all associated personal data at any time. Deletion is <strong>permanent and irreversible</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h2>1. How to delete your account</h2>\n  <h3>Option 1 — In the App (recommended)</h3>\n  <p>Go to <strong>Settings → Delete Account</strong> in the SLP Command app and follow the confirmation steps. Your account is scheduled for permanent deletion immediately upon confirmation.</p>\n\n  <h3>Option 2 — By email</h3>\n  <p>Send a request from your account email address to <a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com?subject=Delete%20my%20account\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a> with the subject line <strong>\"Delete my account\"</strong>, including your account email in the message body for identity verification. We will process verified requests within <strong>30 days</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. What is permanently removed</h2>\n  <p>Upon account deletion, the following is permanently and irreversibly deleted:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Your profile and account, and your login credentials.</li>\n    <li>All Speaking audio recordings and their storage-layer copies.</li>\n    <li>All written responses and AI-generated transcripts.</li>\n    <li>All your attempts, progress, scores and estimated levels across all four skills — Reading, Listening, Writing and Speaking.</li>\n    <li>All Adaptive Coach and Intelligence Dashboard data derived from your results.</li>\n    <li>All support requests submitted through \"Report a Problem\" that have already been resolved at the time of deletion.</li>\n    <li>Your authentication account with our identity provider, so you can no longer sign in with those credentials.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p><strong>What is not affected.</strong> The general content and exercise catalogue of the Service — question banks, listening audio content, reading texts, exercise prompts, and similar shared material that is not specific to your account — is not personal data about you and is not deleted or altered by your account deletion; it remains part of the Service for other users.</p>\n\n  <h2>3. What may be retained, and why</h2>\n  <p><strong>Security audit trail.</strong> A pseudonymous record of security-relevant account events (login, account creation, account deletion) is retained for <strong>12 months from the date of the event</strong>, as described in full in the <a href=\"/data-retention\">Data Retention Policy</a>. This record does not contain your email, content, or any directly identifying information, and does not prevent your erasure request from being honoured for every other category of data.</p>\n  <p><strong>Subscription/billing records.</strong> If you were ever an SLP Command Professional subscriber, we may retain minimal technical and financial fields of your billing events (product purchased, price, currency, an App Store transaction identifier, dates) — dissociated from your account — where necessary for transaction reconciliation, fraud prevention, handling claims, or compliance with an applicable legal obligation. Every identifier capable of linking those records to you within our systems (your account identifier, and the RevenueCat subscriber identifier, alias and subscriber-attribute fields) is irreversibly removed at the moment your account is deleted. See §3 of the <a href=\"/data-retention\">Data Retention Policy</a> for the precise scope of this record.</p>\n\n  <h2>4. Third-party processors and platforms</h2>\n  <p>Processors that received your Content during your use of the Service (see <a href=\"/subprocessors\">Subprocessors and Third Parties</a>) are contractually bound to delete or dissociate it from you in accordance with their data processing agreements with us. Some processors (notably AI providers) may retain transient API request logs for a short period under their own security/abuse-prevention policies, independent of our systems; this is disclosed in the Privacy Policy and does not extend the retention of any data within our own infrastructure.</p>\n  <p><strong>Your Apple subscription is not cancelled by deleting your SLP Command account.</strong> Because your Professional subscription, if any, is billed and administered by Apple through your Apple ID, deleting your SLP Command account or uninstalling the app does <strong>not</strong> cancel it. If you have an active subscription, cancel it separately from your Apple ID account settings (Settings → [your name] → Subscriptions) to stop future renewals — see §10 of the <a href=\"/terms\">Terms of Service</a>.</p>\n\n  <h2>5. Your rights</h2>\n  <p>Account deletion exercises your right to erasure under GDPR Art.&nbsp;17. For other data rights (access, portability, rectification), contact <a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a> or see the <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>\n\n  <h2>6. Contact</h2>\n  <p><a href=\"mailto:privacy@slpcommand.com\">privacy@slpcommand.com</a></p>\n\n  <footer class=\"page-footer\">\n    <a href=\"/\">← SLP Command</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Not affiliated with NATO or any official body.\n  </footer>";

